uture that  it laid out and then they would start to  acquire Bitcoin but these were all  pretty much retail investors there were  no major financial institutions there  were no public companies there were no  Sovereign wealth funds or any type of  large institutional asset allocators  those individuals for about 13 years  they continue to just dollar costs  average into Bitcoin they were using it  as a reserve asset and therefore we had  these really nice clean boom and bust  Cycles the price of Bitcoin acted like  the marketing department as the price  went up more people heard about Bitcoin  and they would come in and they would  try to buy some of it of course it would  get overheated there would be a crash  and then some of the people would get  flushed out but this cycle repeated over  and over again when it was just retailed  but then of course once the pandemic hit  and the central bank and politicians  started step in and intervene in the  market and they were able to inject  trillions of dollars into the economy  and they were able to manipulate  interest rates down to a zero percent  interest rate environment now all of a  sudden Traders and these technocrats  they needed to go find a new asset Paul  Tudor Jones Stanley drucken Miller and  many other Legends of Wall Street at the  end of 2020 started talking about  Bitcoin as an inflation hedge asset they  stated that it would be the fastest  [ __ ] course in that inflation hedge  asset bucket that's exactly what  happened as those Traders came in and as  those technocrats came in they simply  viewed Bitcoin as a risk asset now as  Michael so eloquently pointed out they  got more cash than the retail investors  those retail investors don't care though  they continue to just dollar cost  average into Bitcoin whether the price  is up or down but the Traders and  technocrats they care more than just  about Bitcoin they obviously look at the  underlying fundamentals and the market  dynamics but they're also looking at  things like the interest rate and so as  we headed into the end of 2021 as the  central bankers and many pundits on  mainstream media started talking about  the Federal Reserve increasing interest  rates a lot of those Traders a lot of  those technocrats they said oh my God  risk assets are not going to do well in  a higher interest rate environment they  started to sell all those risk assets  they went risk off and because they  treat Bitcoin like a risk asset they all  started to sell Bitcoin as well now  that's great if you're just a bitcoiner  and you simply are a reach tell person  who continues the dollar cost average  means you're picking up cheaper Bitcoin  today than you were three or four months  ago but of course that means the prices  come down because those Traders and  those technocrats they continue to dump  Bitcoin because they simply go with the  whims of the short-term Market sentiment  and so naturally what's gonna happen  here is as the FED continues to raise  interest rates my guess is that Bitcoin  will trade sideways or down it'll  continue to suffer because a lot of  those Traders and those technocrats  they're selling and they don't plan to  stop but over time eventually the  Traders and technocrats they run out of  Bitcoin to sell sure they got a lot of  money but naturally they can't sell  forever and so they're just simply  transitioning that Bitcoin from  short-term weekends to long-term strong  hands and once the bitcoiners get  control of Bitcoin once they still have  that Bitcoin and they don't move it for  a year or more which right now about 65  percent of Bitcoin is then all of a  sudden you get in an environment where  you get an illiquid market supply and  you simply need some sort of short-term  Catalyst to make the price explode  upwards we saw this happen at the end of  2020 and my guess is that we're going to  see it happen again in the next 24  months or so but right now we're in this  transition period where the Traders and  technocrats they're dumping Bitcoin they  don't want any risk assets they want to  go buy things like Berkshire Hathaway  and value stocks but while they're doing  that the bitcoiners are just picking up  cheap Bitcoin they're making the market  more and more illiquid we continue to  see Bitcoin pulled off of exchanges we  continue to see bitcoiners holding with  strong hands they're not selling they're  handing the Bitcoin to their grandkids  and ultimately the bitcoiners will get  control of this Market again the Bulls  will be in control and the Traders and  technocrats they'll learn a long-term  lesson that bitcoin's not a trading  asset Bitcoin is a store of value it  literally is built to survive high  inflation environments holding Bitcoin  over the next 10 to 20 years is likely  to be one of the easiest things people  can do  the Traders and the technocrats might  learn this lesson the hard way hey you  did you like this video great we make  five of them a day and post them here on  this channel make sure you subscribe  like the video and see you next time
 

